# Drafted by Gemini (R16 deep), edited.

~ arrive
Narrator: A thick yellow-green haze pools at the bottom of the shaft, reeking of wet rot. The tunnel walls are soft and slick, squirming whenever your lantern light touches them.
set sk_deep_seen
quest skitter_plague the_hags_lair
-> END

~ miasma_a
Narrator: The yellow-green haze thickens around your boots, heavy and sour on the tongue.
check Constitution DC 16 -> a_ok | a_fail

~ a_ok
Narrator: You hold your breath and press a sleeve hard across your mouth until the worst of the drift passes.
set sk_miasma_a
-> END

~ a_fail
Narrator: The foul vapour slips past your teeth and coats your throat like warm tallow, setting your chest aching.
damage 1d6 poison party
set sk_miasma_a
-> END

~ miasma_b
Narrator: Nearer the great bronze door, the bilious fog hangs thicker still, stinging your eyes and skin.
check Constitution DC 16 -> b_ok | b_fail

~ b_ok
Narrator: You keep your head low and your lungs shut tight against the creeping reek.
set sk_miasma_b
-> END

~ b_fail
Narrator: You draw a shallow breath of the rot-sweet gas, and black bile rises hot in your throat.
damage 1d6 poison party
set sk_miasma_b
-> END

~ sigils
if flag.skitter_sigils_broken
Narrator: The knotted ring of entrails lies cold and slack upon the stone, its foul breath spent.
-> END
endif
Narrator: Coils of wet sinew and knotted entrails writhe in a wide ring across the chamber floor. With every slow pulse, the glistening meat sweats out a fresh cloud of yellow-green miasma.
-> sigils_menu

~ sigils_menu
* [Athletics DC 17] Hack the ring to pieces -> smash_ok | smash_fail
* [Arcana DC 20] Unpick the working -> unpick_ok | unpick_fail
* [knows:dispel_magic] Cast Dispel Magic at it -> dispel
* [if item:alchemists_fire] Throw Alchemist's Fire -> burn
* Leave it -> END

~ smash_ok
Narrator: Steel bites clean through the knotted gristle, parting the pulsing cords in a spray of dark ichor.
-> sigils_done

~ smash_fail
Narrator: Your blows bounce off the tough, slick sinew without leaving so much as a nick.
-> sigils_menu

~ unpick_ok
Narrator: You trace the crooked binding to its anchor knot and draw the foul thread loose.
-> sigils_done

~ unpick_fail
Narrator: The wet cords twist under your fingers, and the knot only tightens with a wet hiss.
-> sigils_menu

~ dispel
Narrator: Your word of unmaking snaps the unseen tether holding the meat to its rhythm.
-> sigils_done

~ burn
take alchemists_fire
Narrator: The flask shatters and pale green flame crawls greedily over the ring, crisping the wet sinew.
-> sigils_done

~ sigils_done
Narrator: The ring slackens and dies upon the stone, and the hissing gas ceases at once. Far off in the dark of the mine, something lets out a long, wet shriek, as though a blade had found its ribs.
set skitter_sigils_broken
set skitterdeep_alert = now
if flag.stonoga_slain
quest skitter_plague exterminated
set plague_lifted
cutscene sk_plague_lifts
cutscene sk_plague_lifts_2
cutscene end
Narrator: Within the hour, the fever breaks across Wickermoor, and the last of the centipedes scatter into the cold hills.
endif
-> END
